   ("The first-aid box", ["Contents: antiseptics (iodine, Dettol), cotton wool, gauze and roller bandages, adhesive plasters, scissors and tweezers, sterile dressings, burn gel, a clinical thermometer, paracetamol, oral rehydration salts and a first-aid manual. Keep it in a labelled, dry place, restock after each use, and know how to use every item."]),
   ("Common kitchen accidents and first aid", ["<b>Burns and scalds</b> — cool under running water for 10–20 minutes, remove rings/watches (if not stuck), cover with a clean non-stick dressing, never apply butter, ice or ointment, and seek help for large or deep burns. <b>Cuts</b> — wash, apply pressure with a clean cloth, bandage, and see a doctor for deep cuts. <b>Choking</b> — encourage coughing; give the back blows and the Heimlich manoeuvre. <b>Falls and faints</b> — keep the person lying, raise the legs, call for help. <b>Electric shock</b> — switch off the power first; never touch the person with bare hands."]),
